","H1870":"conduct","H3045":"to know","H1931":"he/she/it","H3474":"to smooth","H734":"way","H1961":"to be","H2450":"wise","H3372":"to fear","H853":"[Obj.]","H5493":"remove","H7451":"harmful","H7500":"healing","H8270":"umbilical cord","H8250":"drink","H6106":"bone","H3513":"honour","H1952":"substance","H7225":"beginning","H8393":"produce","H4390":"to fill","H618":"storehouse","H7647":"abundance","H8492":"new wine","H3342":"wine","H6555":"to break through","H4148":"discipline","H3988":"to reject","H6973":"to loathe","H8433":"rebuke","H834":"which","H157":"lover","H3198":"to rebuke","H1":"father","H7521":"to accept","H835":"blessed","H2451":"wisdom","H6329":"to promote","H8394":"understanding","H5504":"profit","H5505":"merchandise","H3701":"money","H2742":"sharp","H3368":"precious","H6443":"jewel","H2656":"pleasure","H3808":"not","H7737":"be like","H3225":"right","H8040":"left","H6239":"riches","H3519":"glory","H5278":"pleasantness","H5410":"path","H6086":"wood","H2388":"strengthen","H8551":"to grasp","H833":"to bless","H3245":"to found","H776":"country/planet","H3559":"prepare","H8064":"heaven","H1847":"knowledge","H8415":"abyss","H1234":"to break up/open","H7834":"cloud","H7491":"to drip","H2919":"dew","H3868":"be devious","H8454":"wisdom","H4209":"plot","H5315":"soul","H227":"then","H3212":"to walk","H983":"security","H7272":"foot","H5062":"to strike","H518":"if","H7901":"lay down","H6342":"to dread","H6149":"to please","H8142":"sleep","H6343":"dread","H6597":"suddenly","H7722":"ravage","H7563":"wicked","H935":"come","H3689":"loin","H8104":"obey","H3921":"capture","H4513":"to withhold","H1167":"master","H410":"God","H3027":"hand","H6213":"do","H559":"to say","H7453":"neighbor","H7725":"return","H4279":"tomorrow","H5414":"give","H3426":"there","H854":"with","H2790":"to plow/plot","H3427":"to dwell","H7378":"to contend","H5973":"with","H2600":"for nothing","H1580":"to wean","H7065":"be jealous","H376":"man","H2555":"violence","H977":"to choose","H8441":"abomination","H3477":"upright","H5475":"counsel","H3994":"curse","H1004":"place","H5116":"pasture","H6662":"righteous","H1288":"to bless","H3887":"to mock","H6041":"afflicted","H6035":"poor","H5157":"to inherit","H3684":"fool","H7311":"to exalt","H7036":"dishonor"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","My son. God speaks, or the master instructs his disciple, ver. 21. (Calmet) — We must remember and love instruction, and reduce it to practice. (Worthington)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Peace. These prefigured more substantial blessings. (Calmet)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Truth. Be kind and faithful to all, Genesis xxiv. 27., and Psalm xxiv. 10."],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Good. Septuagint, “forecast good before the Lord and men.” St. Paul seems to allude to this version, Romans xii. 17., and 2 Corinthians viii. 22. (Haydock)"],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","All. God will have nothing by halves. — Lean not. By pride, 2 Corinthians xii. 13. All must be referred to God. (Calmet) — In him we may safely trust. (Worthington)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Bones. Thou shalt enjoy perfect health."],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Fruits. Septuagint add, “of justice;” to intimate that no presents will be acceptable, which have been unjustly acquired."],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Him. Correction is rather a proof of love than of anger, Psalm iii. 19. (Calmet) — God thus shews that he approves of his servants; and therefore his other promises, which seem of a temporal nature, must be understood with reference to the next life. (Worthington)"],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","And as. Septuagint, “but he scourgeth every son whom he receiveth,” as St. Paul quotes this passage, Hebrews xii. 6. The verb is now wanting in Hebrew, or ceab; “as a father” may signify “scourgeth, in piel, (Menochius) with i prefixed. (Calmet)"],["haydock",15,null,"haydock","Riches. Hebrew peninim, (Haydock) “pearls,” Job xxviii. 18. (Calmet)"],["haydock",16,null,"haydock","Glory. Her hands are full, and she grants favours with profusion, (Haydock) as with both hands, promising eternal life. (Worthington)"],["haydock",18,null,"haydock","Life. Like that planted in paradise, Genesis ii. 9."],["haydock",19,null,"haydock","Wisdom. Hitherto he had spoken of that virtue. Now he treats of the uncreated wisdom, (Calmet) which is God the Son. (Menochius) (Jansenius) (St. Gregory, Mor. xii. 4.)"],["haydock",20,null,"haydock","Out. The higher and lower waters being divided, (Calmet) or the channels formed to receive the waters. (Piscator) — It may also speak of the deluge. (Ven. Bede) — With. Hebrew, “have distilled dew.” This is so copious, as to resemble rain in Palestine, Judges vi. 37., and 2 Kings xvii. 12."],["haydock",22,null,"haydock","Mouth. There have been wise and virtuous men afflicted, ver. 11. But they have borne all with patience, and have merited a more glorious reward than what this earth could afford. (Calmet)"],["haydock",27,null,"haydock","Able. Protestants, “withhold not good from them to whom it is due, when it is in the power of thine hand to do it.” Relieve the distressed. (Haydock) — They have a title to that wealth, since those who possess it are bound to relieve the indigent. (Calmet) — Septuagint, “refrain not from doing good,” &c. (Haydock)"],["haydock",28,null,"haydock","Present. Alms in season are doubly valuable. (Worthington) — Antigonus acquired the title of Doson, “about to give,” as he never gave, (Plutarch) but only promised."],["haydock",30,null,"haydock","Cause. We may defend ourselves; but herein great discretion is necessary. (Calmet) — Cum pari contendere anceps est: cum superiore furiosum; cum inferiore sordidum. (Seneca, Prov.)"],["haydock",31,null,"haydock","Ways. Of injustice. Seek not to attain his prosperity by the same means. (Calmet)"],["haydock",33,null,"haydock","Want. Hebrew, “a curse.” — Shall be. Hebrew, “he blesseth.” (Haydock)"],["haydock",34,null,"haydock","Scorners. Literally, “he will delude the scorners.” (Haydock) — He will treat them as they would treat others, Psalm xvii. 27. (Calmet) — Septuagint, “the Lord resisteth the proud,” &c. So the apostles quote this passage, 1 Peter v. 5., and James iv. 6. (Haydock)"],["haydock",35,null,"haydock","Disgrace. They are seen by more, and their fall is more dangerous. (Calmet) — “A fool extols what is ignominious.” (Pagnin) (Haydock)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}